  {
    "text": "Latest official plugin card status from the user’s clicks. These are status facts, not a request for more work. applied means the plugin is enabled now; restart-required means it is saved and takes effect after DSH restarts; overridden means another configuration keeps it off; failed or cancelled means it is not enabled and can be retried from its card; already-enabled means it was on already; dismissed means the user declined it, so do not offer it again in this conversation. Enabling a plugin authorizes nothing beyond it. Continue with the user’s current request.
